    "Jhn"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "And the third day there was a marriage in Cana of Galilee; and the mother of Jesus was there:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And both Jesus was called, and his disciples, to the marriage.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "And when they wanted wine, the mother of Jesus saith unto him, They have no wine.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Jesus saith unto her, Woman, what have I to do with thee? mine hour is not yet come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "His mother saith unto the servants, Whatsoever he saith unto you, do it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And there were set there six waterpots of stone, after the manner of the purifying of the Jews, containing two or three firkins apiece.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Jesus saith unto them, Fill the waterpots with water. And they filled them up to the brim.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And he saith unto them, Draw out now, and bear unto the governor of the feast. And they bare it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "When the ruler of the feast had tasted the water that was made wine, and knew not whence it was: (but the servants which drew the water knew;) the governor of the feast called the bridegroom,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "And saith unto him, Every man at the beginning doth set forth good wine; and when men have well drunk, then that which is worse: but thou hast kept the good wine until now.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "This beginning of miracles did Jesus in Cana of Galilee, and manifested forth his glory; and his disciples believed on him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "After this he went down to Capernaum, he, and his mother, and his brethren, and his disciples: and they continued there not many days.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "And the Jews’ passover was at hand, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "And found in the temple those that sold oxen and sheep and doves, and the changers of money sitting:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And when he had made a scourge of small cords, he drove them all out of the temple, and the sheep, and the oxen; and poured out the changers’ money, and overthrew the tables;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And said unto them that sold doves, Take these things hence; make not my Father’s house an house of merchandise.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And his disciples remembered that it was written, The zeal of thine house hath eaten me up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Then answered the Jews and said unto him, What sign shewest thou unto us, seeing that thou doest these things?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Jesus answered and said unto them, Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Then said the Jews, Forty and six years was this temple in building, and wilt thou rear it up in three days?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "But he spake of the temple of his body.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "When therefore he was risen from the dead, his disciples remembered that he had said this unto them; and they believed the scripture, and the word which Jesus had said.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Now when he was in Jerusalem at the passover, in the feast day, many believed in his name, when they saw the miracles which he did.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "But Jesus did not commit himself unto them, because he knew all men,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:2:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "And needed not that any should testify of man: for he knew what was in man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 2:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:2:25"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "repository": "aruljohn/Bible-kjv",
